# Duskara is free (Milestone 25c; like nordveil_victory.scene). The party
# walks up from the gate as the town spills out around the brimming oasis.

spawn {a1} {a1} at 15,18 facing up
spawn {a2} {a2} at 17,18 facing up
spawn {a3} {a3} at 16,19 facing up
music town
move player to 16,12 async
move {a1} to 15,13 async
move {a2} to 17,13 async
move {a3} to 16,14 async
spawn kid1 child at 5,15 facing up
spawn neighbor1 worker at 22,16 facing up
spawn neighbor2 merchant at 6,4 facing down
move kid1 to 12,12 async
move neighbor1 to 20,12 async
move neighbor2 to 13,10 async
sync
face player up
emote kid1 heart
emote neighbor1 note
say Water-Keeper: Feel that wind? It's cool. It's actually cool! The heat is broken.
say Water-Keeper: The oasis came back the moment the Tyrant fell - water pushing up through the cracked mud like it had been waiting.
emote player note
say Guard: We'll have that buried house dug out by sundown. And tonight we drink well water until we can't stand.
say Child: The water's cold! Come and feel it!
emote frank note
say Frank: Two kingdoms breathing again. You four are getting good at this.
say Frank: That leaves Selavon, out on the eastern coast. The Drowned Admiral has it locked in a storm that never ends. But that's a problem for another day.
say Water-Keeper: Duskara's wells and gates are yours, always. Rest. Eat. Let the smith fit you with Sunsteel.
